---
description: Dismiss adds window listeners only while an element is open, so a closed popover, menu, or panel costs nothing.
---

## Basic

Use the `dismiss` action on a custom panel to close it when the user clicks outside. Set `enabled` to the open state so the action adds the `window` listener only while the panel is open. Pass `type: "click"` with a `handler` that closes the panel when the click lands outside it.

The panel's own trigger is also outside the panel, so the handler ignores clicks on the trigger and lets the trigger toggle the state.

<FileSource src="/framed/Dismiss/DismissBasic" />

## Multiple listeners

Pass `listeners` to attach more than one listener, each with its own `type` and `handler`. Combine a `keydown` listener with a `click` listener to close the panel on <DocKbd label="Escape" /> and on an outside click.

Listeners with the same `type` and options share one `window` listener across every control on the page.

<FileSource src="/framed/Dismiss/DismissMultiple" />

## Timing

The action registers its listeners after a macrotask, not synchronously. Enabling it inside a click, such as a button that sets `open` to `true`, therefore never dismisses the panel with the same click that opened it.

[Dropdown](/components/Dropdown) closes on outside click with this action, so a custom panel behaves the same way.
